Question: 3033. Modify the Matrix
Given a 0-indexed m x n integer matrix matrix, create a new 0-indexed matrix called answer. Make answer equal to matrix, then replace each element with
the value -1 with the maximum element in its respective column.Return the matrix answer.

Explanation :
This was an easy question where I ran two for loops insde another loop, the first one was to calulate the maximum of current column and the second one was 
to update '-1' with the local maximum.

Solution :
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> modifiedMatrix(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {
        int mx,m=matrix.size(),n=matrix[0].size();
        for(int j=0;j<n;j++){
            mx=INT_MIN;
            for(int i=0;i<m;i++){
                if(matrix[i][j]>mx){
                    mx=matrix[i][j];
                }
            }
            for(int i=0;i<m;i++){
                if(matrix[i][j]==-1){
                    matrix[i][j]=mx;
                }
            }
        }
        return matrix;
    }
};
